# Local static build outputs. `build.sh` writes fstool, fstool-nopie and
# fstool-stats beside the source tree; experiment variants (fstool-goldmont,
# fstool-lto, …) land there too. These are ~14 MB rebuilt artefacts, not
# source: the companion tree under ~/dev/fstool-build owns the build recipe,
# and the deployed copies live on the target hosts.
/fstool
/fstool-*
